## Rules

- Split the span into 3–6 sections, each with a `role`: exactly one `hook` (the opening), exactly one `payoff` (the close), the rest `build` / `reset`.
- Assign each section its visuals (`image_refs`) — one visual at most once across the WHOLE outline; the hook section gets the visual whose subject matches the opening phrase; the strongest visual belongs to the payoff.
- Anchor each section with its opening words (`marker`, verbatim from the cue lines) + optional `approx_start` seconds. The first section starts at the span start by construction. You never write `start`/`end`.
- `arc` = one line: the emotional journey. `note` per section = what this section does for the arc.

